{{R:wversity}}
[[File:Earthquake Richter Scale.jpg|thumb|''Richter scale'' chart.]]

===Etymology===
From American seismologist {{w|Charles Richter}}, whose name derives from {{der|en|de|Richter|t=judge}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{audio|en|En-us-Richter scale.ogg|Audio (US)}}

===Proper noun===
{{en-proper noun}}

# {{lb|en|seismology}} a [[logarithmic]] [[scale]] used to [[express]] the [[energy]] released by an [[earthquake]], each [[increase]] of 1 representing a 32-fold increase in energy.

